[{:db/id "q-4016/selection/0c74d87ed8edc44ababbd912c039546035c718e66a9a0c2b1a2014abc154062d" :answer/id #uuid "e865fe4b-b552-5e49-96e0-af34995f5e9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-{e}^{x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4016/selection/5fbd5e9ff4a6c55b5a51212b901701b48190ce2573eceab80ad793c99a102454" :answer/id #uuid "b5b377a4-5170-5909-969a-fee5feb2b631" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{x}+1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4016/selection/28e5bf8349ca30d7f7c52d8b79df09326546df28b22ae224819d9968776e86ef" :answer/id #uuid "dd92b623-ea95-5559-b407-a6917af8dcc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4016/selection/c3cb9962a2a2ebf0e9c1969cb6f4c3280d8dfa71380bf1d27e7e9156b28f9467" :answer/id #uuid "13db39f2-ff13-5346-83b5-dc1e2e7c1488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4016/selection/377c682f00280039f7e30d495fc3b26c1523e96a4ddbb044ecf7f6cf20768f20" :answer/id #uuid "860d2f15-f8dc-50f2-bc1d-877881de2c7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4{e}^{x}-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4016/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e35eb022-54e0-5d0a-b4bd-e9bd48e358a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4016/selection/c3cb9962a2a2ebf0e9c1969cb6f4c3280d8dfa71380bf1d27e7e9156b28f9467" :answer-field/choices ["q-4016/selection/0c74d87ed8edc44ababbd912c039546035c718e66a9a0c2b1a2014abc154062d" "q-4016/selection/5fbd5e9ff4a6c55b5a51212b901701b48190ce2573eceab80ad793c99a102454" "q-4016/selection/28e5bf8349ca30d7f7c52d8b79df09326546df28b22ae224819d9968776e86ef" "q-4016/selection/c3cb9962a2a2ebf0e9c1969cb6f4c3280d8dfa71380bf1d27e7e9156b28f9467" "q-4016/selection/377c682f00280039f7e30d495fc3b26c1523e96a4ddbb044ecf7f6cf20768f20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4016" :question/id #uuid "20669a20-777a-5d15-ade0-e739edb8a182" :question/math-academy-id "q-4016" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2y}} \\\\ {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{2y} & =2{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+C) & =0 \\\\ 2+C & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4016/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4016"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14310/selection/3ef2d882942a45f9dd3bfcbeb9bfa788b6279d4bf324d1867105dcb5a2d05191" :answer/id #uuid "34bd2de0-93c2-5efd-a1fc-6f4f8b5a2dee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14310/selection/54fa0568215cd65d174cc72790a3130c03c5c89fe986eb5551c392ef1d84bd34" :answer/id #uuid "63c160d0-8bc1-5f1d-8441-c1e9e370bed3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14310/selection/3897587c378a13bcfdf1896459e9b2292cf61f51ce86eef37939ff6c20340f94" :answer/id #uuid "5b60de0c-c7aa-599a-8749-99ff0d614957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14310/selection/eac27901c02e1e3a48fd57a2ce1d2d99a0b21ae3f9c64bf4d02cad92141a4103" :answer/id #uuid "54d14098-faa6-5881-afca-5a6442c450e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14310/selection/2b16ed80a4ba9b9ec10a91f38d260e3f42fafca9b37f44b3cc2d90bc080b2de1" :answer/id #uuid "a5595c32-d167-5a2c-9469-972e442fece1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14310/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db7f66ee-621c-5010-bfcb-e5d681c9977f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14310/selection/eac27901c02e1e3a48fd57a2ce1d2d99a0b21ae3f9c64bf4d02cad92141a4103" :answer-field/choices ["q-14310/selection/3ef2d882942a45f9dd3bfcbeb9bfa788b6279d4bf324d1867105dcb5a2d05191" "q-14310/selection/54fa0568215cd65d174cc72790a3130c03c5c89fe986eb5551c392ef1d84bd34" "q-14310/selection/3897587c378a13bcfdf1896459e9b2292cf61f51ce86eef37939ff6c20340f94" "q-14310/selection/eac27901c02e1e3a48fd57a2ce1d2d99a0b21ae3f9c64bf4d02cad92141a4103" "q-14310/selection/2b16ed80a4ba9b9ec10a91f38d260e3f42fafca9b37f44b3cc2d90bc080b2de1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14310" :question/id #uuid "ef4e4fc3-8477-5354-a829-8e34e5c5f42e" :question/math-academy-id "q-14310" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1$ given that  $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y) & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ to find $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C) \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C \\\\ \\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ C & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-14310/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14310"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355544/field-1/5a6349d94d7c41360f13370ca61f6a71021cfb95f5bff66a28bbdbdc3b058016" :answer/id #uuid "2f9fdbbe-6c91-576e-964d-2dfe7094a9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}\\tan(7x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355544/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f08ee092-354d-5b2e-a653-c757d24ab056" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355544/field-1/5a6349d94d7c41360f13370ca61f6a71021cfb95f5bff66a28bbdbdc3b058016" :answer-field/choices ["q-355544/field-1/5a6349d94d7c41360f13370ca61f6a71021cfb95f5bff66a28bbdbdc3b058016"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355544" :question/id #uuid "1adf5c18-652c-5a35-ba00-6bf5024e9f68" :question/math-academy-id "q-355544" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${sec}^{2}⁡(4y){y}^{′}={sec}^{2}⁡(7x)$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{8}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$\n\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡(7x) \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={sec}^{2}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=4{C}_{1}.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(4\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7\\cdot 0)+C \\\\ 0 & =0+C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-355544/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355544"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355546/field-1/defe3de27c2c3bddb1da3649c0b696a614e780ae7dd4601e07fa846cced55a5c" :answer/id #uuid "e83f0dba-a96b-5eef-892c-e7bd97ee16f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x^2-\\frac{5}{x}+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355546/field-1/f11cbe5f5c2191ae073f809e951bf9b0f2aa815b98169ba0b8b4ee77da263228" :answer/id #uuid "63609b85-c6f5-5030-9499-a29f4e473a1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x^2-\\frac{5}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355546/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f30ee74b-194b-5ef8-a522-c1f51f015f52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355546/field-1/defe3de27c2c3bddb1da3649c0b696a614e780ae7dd4601e07fa846cced55a5c" :answer-field/choices ["q-355546/field-1/defe3de27c2c3bddb1da3649c0b696a614e780ae7dd4601e07fa846cced55a5c" "q-355546/field-1/f11cbe5f5c2191ae073f809e951bf9b0f2aa815b98169ba0b8b4ee77da263228"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355546" :question/id #uuid "26f23820-0414-5dbe-a547-4bdb9a3bb271" :question/math-academy-id "q-355546" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3}=5$ that satisfies $y(1)=6.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5+8{x}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=6$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =6 \\\\ -5(1)^{-1}+4(1)^{2}+C & =6 \\\\ C-1 & =6 \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x}+4{x}^{2}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-355546/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355546"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
